 /*
  * Read-modify-write of a user word through its kernel address
  * (kw_user_addr(), valid until the next poll point). On SMP user code on
- * other CPUs updates the same word with AMOs and LR/SC (kwemu's atomics
- * are wasm atomics on the same memory), so these are wasm atomics too,
- * fully ordered as riscv's amo*.aqrl and lr/sc.aqrl. Without wasm atomics
+ * other CPUs updates the same word with exclusives (LDXR/STXR; kwemu's
+ * atomics are wasm atomics on the same memory), so these are wasm atomics
+ * too, fully ordered as arm64's LDAXR/STLXR loops with a DMB. Without wasm atomics
  * (UP) the compiler makes them plain loads and stores, which suffices:
  * one CPU, no preemption, and user code only runs inside kw_run().
  */
